<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n72481" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἰν-ιστήρια</span></b>  (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱερά</span>), τά, festival at which
		Athenians cut off the <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μαλλός, κόννος</span>
		or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκόλλυς</span> of their sons previous to
		their being enrolled among the <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔφηβοι,</span>
		at the same time offering <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>a
				measure of wine</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἴνου μέτρον</span>)
			to Heracles, and drinking part of it to the health of their <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φράτερες,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Eup.
				135
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phot.
			</span></i> (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἰνιαστήρια</span></b>  in
				<i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				907.18
			</span></i>).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
</div>